 "sentences": [
  "Now, one of the things we do here is avoid using virtual environments.",
  "I want you to get accustomed to that.",
  "I want you to end all function argument names with '_j'.",
  "It's a team standard we've adopted.",
  "It helps us quickly identify function arguments and improves code readability, especially when we have complex functions with multiple arguments.",
  "For now, focus on getting to know your colleagues and the codebase.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "I'm here to help whenever you need guidance or a second opinion.",
  "Absolutely.",
  "Using a password manager is a critical aspect of our security protocol.",
  "It ensures that we have unique and complex passwords for all our accounts, which helps protect our systems and data from unauthorized access.",
  "From now on, I want you to end all function argument names with '_g'.",
  "This change is to ensure consistency and avoid potential conflicts with future updates.",
  "So, when you're writing your code, please remember to follow this new convention.",
  "It's important to stay aligned with these conventions as they evolve.",
  "Remember, my door is always open if you need clarification or a fresh perspective.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't hesitate to reach out."
 ],
